-- title:
--   Finite freeness of A[[X]]/(f₁,…,f_d) over an Artinian local ring
-- statement:
--   Let $A$ be a commutative local Artinian ring, let $k$ be a field, and let $\mathrm{res} \colon A \to k$ be a surjective ring homomorphism. Let $d$ be a natural number and let $f \colon \mathrm{Fin}\,d \to A[[X_1,\dots,X_d]]$ be a family of $d$ multivariate formal power series in $d$ variables over $A$, each with vanishing constant coefficient. Write $\bar f_i =$ the coefficientwise image of $f_i$ under $\mathrm{res}$, an element of $k[[X_1,\dots,X_d]]$. Assume that the quotient of $k[[X_1,\dots,X_d]]$ by the ideal generated by the set of all $\bar f_i$ is a finite (that is, finitely generated) $k$-module. The conclusion is the conjunction of three assertions about the quotient $M = A[[X_1,\dots,X_d]] / (f_1,\dots,f_d)$, where the ideal is the span of the range of $f$: that $M$ is a finite $A$-module, that $M$ is a free $A$-module, and that its $A$-rank $\mathrm{finrank}_A M$ equals the $k$-dimension $\mathrm{finrank}_k\bigl(k[[X_1,\dots,X_d]]/(\bar f_1,\dots,\bar f_d)\bigr)$.
--
--   This is the standard flatness-and-rank statement for a $d$-tuple of power series without constant term in $d$ variables over an Artinian local base: finiteness of the fibre over the residue field propagates to finiteness, freeness and constancy of rank over the base, the field case resting on miracle flatness for the substitution endomorphism of $k[[X_1,\dots,X_d]]$ ([`MvPowerSeries.finite_flat_exists_basis_substAlgHom_of_finite_quotient`](thm.html#MvPowerSeries.finite_flat_exists_basis_substAlgHom_of_finite_quotient), together with the identification of the ideal generated by the variables as the kernel of the constant-coefficient map, [`MvPowerSeries.span_range_X_eq_ker_constantCoeff`](thm.html#MvPowerSeries.span_range_X_eq_ker_constantCoeff)). It is used in the treatment of formal modules over Artinian local rings in the Čerednik–Drinfeld part of the development, namely in [`CerednikDrinfeld.FormalODModule.isSpecial_and_hasHeight_four_of_isIso_of_isArtinianRing`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.FormalODModule.isSpecial_and_hasHeight_four_of_isIso_of_isArtinianRing) and [`CerednikDrinfeld.SpecialFormal.Rigidified.exists_isAdmissible_and_isIsomorphic_iff_exists_isIso_of_isArtinianRing`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.SpecialFormal.Rigidified.exists_isAdmissible_and_isIsomorphic_iff_exists_isIso_of_isArtinianRing).
